  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish several relevant directions: elevated-temperature indentation and tribology of HEA films (R2), temperature-dependent wear of HEAs (R3), and atomistic temperature-dependent deformation of FCC HEAs involving dislocations, stacking faults, and increasing HCP fractions (especially R4 and R16, with supporting evidence from R13 and R15). They therefore point toward coupling temperature, defect evolution, phase/local-order changes, and mechanical or frictional response. However, none describes the specific FeNiCrCoCu coating-on-Cu system or combines finite-temperature molecular-dynamics nanoindentation and sliding friction with the reported high-temperature transition from stacking-fault-mediated deformation to lattice disorder and dislocation-density loss. Selecting that coated geometry, combined intervention, and threshold-like mechanism would still require a substantial new idea."
